{"id":"mahabharata-3-121","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":121,"title":"एकविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 121 · The fords of Payoshni and the sacrifices of kings","summary":{"en":"At the Payoshni Lomasha tells of King Nriga, whose Soma intoxicated Indra, and of King Gaya, whose sacrificial posts covered the earth. Yudhishthira asks how the sage Chyavana made the Ashvins drinkers of Soma.","kn":"ಪಯೋಷ್ಣಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಲೋಮಶರು ಸೋಮದಿಂದ ಇಂದ್ರನನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೇರಿಸಿದ ನೃಗರಾಜನನ್ನೂ, ಯಜ್ಞಸ್ತಂಭಗಳು ಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನೇ ಮುಚ್ಚಿದ ಗಯರಾಜನನ್ನೂ ಕುರಿತು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಚ್ಯವನ ಋಷಿ ಅಶ್ವಿನೀದೇವತೆಗಳನ್ನು ಸೋಮಪಾಯಿಗಳನ್ನಾಗಿ ಹೇಗೆ ಮಾಡಿದರು ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पयोष्णी पर लोमश राजा नृग की बात सुनाते हैं, जिनके सोम से इन्द्र मत्त हुए, और राजा गय की, जिनके यज्ञ-स्तम्भों ने पृथ्वी ढक दी। युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि ऋषि च्यवन ने अश्विनीकुमारों को सोमपायी कैसे बनाया।","te":"పయోష్ణి వద్ద లోమశుడు సోమంతో ఇంద్రుని మత్తెక్కించిన నృగరాజు గురించి, యజ్ఞస్తంభాలతో భూమిని కప్పిన గయరాజు గురించి చెబుతాడు. చ్యవన మహర్షి అశ్వినీదేవతలను సోమపానార్హులుగా ఎలా చేశాడని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"பயோஷ்ணியில் லோமஶர், தன் ஸோமத்தால் இந்திரனை மயக்கிய ந்ருக மன்னனையும், வேள்வித் தூண்களால் பூமியை மூடிய கய மன்னனையும் பற்றிச் சொல்கிறார். ச்யவன முனிவர் அஶ்வினிகளை ஸோமம் அருந்துவோராக எப்படி ஆக்கினார் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்கிறார்.","ml":"പയോഷ്ണിയുടെ തീരത്ത് ലോമശൻ നൃഗരാജാവിനെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ സോമരസം ഇന്ദ്രനെ ലഹരിപിടിപ്പിച്ചു. ഗയരാജാവിനെക്കുറിച്ചും, അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ യാഗസ്തംഭങ്ങൾ ഭൂമിയെ മുഴുവൻ മൂടിയതും ലോമശൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. ച്യവനമുനി എങ്ങനെയാണ് അശ്വിനികളെ സോമപാനത്തിന് അർഹരാക്കിയതെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.121; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नृगेण यजमानेन सोमेनेह पुरंदरः ।\nतर्पितः श्रूयते राजन्स तृप्तो मदमभ्यगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, it is told that here Nriga, performing a sacrifice, satisfied Indra with soma, and Indra, content, grew exhilarated."}},{"n":2,"text":"इह देवैः सहेन्द्रैर्हि प्रजापतिभिरेव च ।\nइष्टं बहुविधैर्यज्ञैर्महद्भिर्भूरिदक्षिणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here the gods with Indra and the Prajapatis performed many kinds of great sacrifices with abundant gifts."}},{"n":3,"text":"आमूर्तरयसश्चेह राजा वज्रधरं प्रभुम् ।\nतर्पयामास सोमेन हयमेधेषु सप्तसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"And here King Amurtarayas gratified the lord who wields the thunderbolt with soma at seven horse sacrifices."}},{"n":4,"text":"तस्य सप्तसु यज्ञेषु सर्वमासीद्धिरण्मयम् ।\nवानस्पत्यं च भौमं च यद्द्रव्यं नियतं मखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At those seven sacrifices everything was of gold, both the objects of wood and those of earth that are fixed in a sacrifice."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेष्वेव चास्य यज्ञेषु प्रयोगाः सप्त विश्रुताः ।\nसप्तैकैकस्य यूपस्य चषालाश्चोपरि स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At those same sacrifices seven famous rites were performed, and on each sacrificial post seven rings were set at the top."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्य स्म यूपान्यज्ञेषु भ्राजमानान्हिरण्मयान् ।\nस्वयमुत्थापयामासुर्देवाः सेन्द्रा युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, the gods with Indra themselves raised up his shining golden posts at those sacrifices."}},{"n":7,"text":"तेषु तस्य मखाग्र्येषु गयस्य पृथिवीपतेः ।\nअमाद्यदिन्द्रः सोमेन दक्षिणाभिर्द्विजातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At those excellent sacrifices of King Gaya, Indra grew exhilarated with soma, and the brahmins with their fees."}},{"n":8,"text":"सिकता वा यथा लोके यथा वा दिवि तारकाः ।\nयथा वा वर्षतो धारा असंख्येयाश्च केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the sands of the world, or the stars in the sky, or the streams of falling rain, which no one can count,"}},{"n":9,"text":"तथैव तदसंख्येयं धनं यत्प्रददौ गयः ।\nसदस्येभ्यो महाराज तेषु यज्ञेषु सप्तसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"so uncountable was the wealth that Gaya gave to the assembled priests at those seven sacrifices, great king."}},{"n":10,"text":"भवेत्संख्येयमेतद्वै यदेतत्परिकीर्तितम् ।\nन सा शक्या तु संख्यातुं दक्षिणा दक्षिणावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What has been described here might perhaps be counted, but the fee of that generous giver could not be."}},{"n":11,"text":"हिरण्मयीभिर्गोभिश्च कृताभिर्विश्वकर्मणा ।\nब्राह्मणांस्तर्पयामास नानादिग्भ्यः समागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With cows of gold made by Vishvakarma he satisfied the brahmins who had come from every quarter."}},{"n":12,"text":"अल्पावशेषा पृथिवी चैत्यैरासीन्महात्मनः ।\nगयस्य यजमानस्य तत्र तत्र विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth, for the great-souled Gaya as he sacrificed, was left with little room, so crowded was it with shrines here and there, lord of the people."}},{"n":13,"text":"स लोकान्प्राप्तवानैन्द्रान्कर्मणा तेन भारत ।\nसलोकतां तस्य गच्छेत्पयोष्ण्यां य उपस्पृशेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that deed, Bharata, he won the worlds of Indra. Whoever bathes in the Payoshni will attain the same world as his."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्मात्त्वमत्र राजेन्द्र भ्रातृभिः सहितोऽनघ ।\nउपस्पृश्य महीपाल धूतपाप्मा भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, sinless king, lord of the earth, bathe here with your brothers, and you will be freed from sin."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"स पयोष्ण्यां नरश्रेष्ठः स्नात्वा वै भ्रातृभिः सह ।\nवैडूर्यपर्वतं चैव नर्मदां च महानदीम् ।\nसमाजगाम तेजस्वी भ्रातृभिः सहितोऽनघः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of men bathed in the Payoshni with his brothers. The radiant, sinless king then came with his brothers to the Vaidurya mountain and the great river Narmada."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततोऽस्य सर्वाण्याचख्यौ लोमशो भगवानृषिः ।\nतीर्थानि रमणीयानि तत्र तत्र विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the holy sage Lomasha told him of all the delightful fords found here and there, lord of the people."}},{"n":17,"text":"यथायोगं यथाप्रीति प्रययौ भ्रातृभिः सह ।\nददमानोऽसकृद्वित्तं ब्राह्मणेभ्यः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As seemed fitting and pleasing, he travelled with his brothers, giving wealth again and again to brahmins by the thousand."}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"देवानामेति कौन्तेय तथा राज्ञां सलोकताम् ।\nवैडूर्यपर्वतं दृष्ट्वा नर्मदामवतीर्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, one who sees the Vaidurya mountain and descends into the Narmada reaches the world of the gods and of the kings."}},{"n":19,"text":"संधिरेष नरश्रेष्ठ त्रेताया द्वापरस्य च ।\nएतमासाद्य कौन्तेय सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, this is the junction of the Treta and Dvapara ages. Reaching it, son of Kunti, one is freed from all sins."}},{"n":20,"text":"एष शर्यातियज्ञस्य देशस्तात प्रकाशते ।\nसाक्षाद्यत्रापिबत्सोममश्विभ्यां सह कौशिकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This, dear child, is the place where the sacrifice of Sharyati shines forth, where Kaushika drank soma together with the Ashvins."}},{"n":21,"text":"चुकोप भार्गवश्चापि महेन्द्रस्य महातपाः ।\nसंस्तम्भयामास च तं वासवं च्यवनः प्रभुः ।\nसुकन्यां चापि भार्यां स राजपुत्रीमिवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here too the great ascetic Bhargava Chyavana grew angry at Mahendra, and by his power he paralysed Indra, and he gained Sukanya as his wife, a king's daughter."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"कथं विष्टम्भितस्तेन भगवान्पाकशासनः ।\nकिमर्थं भार्गवश्चापि कोपं चक्रे महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did he paralyse the lord Indra, the punisher of Paka? And why did the greatly ascetic Bhargava grow angry?"}},{"n":23,"text":"नासत्यौ च कथं ब्रह्मन्कृतवान्सोमपीथिनौ ।\nएतत्सर्वं यथावृत्तमाख्यातु भगवान्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how, brahmin, did he make the two Nasatyas drinkers of soma? Let the holy one tell me all this exactly as it happened."}}]}]}